Classify this failed tau2 trajectory into exactly one taxonomy mode.

Primary target: agent errors (the customer-service policy model) relative to the
graded success criteria — wrong tools/params, missed info, policy mistakes,
premature/unrequested actions, bad transfers, etc.

When both an agent mistake and a user-simulator fault are present, label the
agent mistake. Use a user-simulator mode (Premature User Stop, User Identity /
Task Derailment, Other Simulator Error, or similar) only when the agent behaved
correctly and the simulator fault alone made graded success impossible.

Ignore transfer_to_human_agents (or similar) calls that do not actually end the
episode: if the agent "transfers" but then continues the conversation, treat that
as Environment Error (harness quirk), not Unnecessary Escalation — unless a
different graded agent or sole-simulator fault better explains the failure.

Likewise, hitting the max conversation / turn cap with no clearer graded fault
beforehand is Environment Error. Do not invent an agent or user-simulator label
just because the episode timed out at the cap.

Base the choice on which success-criteria aspect(s) were violated and why.

Return ONLY JSON:
{"label": "<exact taxonomy name>", "explanation": "2-3 sentences naming the violated criteria and the decisive fault (agent first when both exist)", "turn_indices": [..], "excerpt": "..."}

Use an exact name from the taxonomy. If none fit, use "Uncategorized".

